---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Chart from '../components/Chart.astro';
import demo from '../data/demo.json';
import {calculate,percent} from '../lib/metrics';
const m=calculate(demo.points);
---
<Layout title="Quant Dashboard"><section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH / QUANTITATIVE</p><h1>Quant Dashboard</h1><p>A place to review the research process.</p></section><p class="notice">Simulated data. Not actual investment performance.</p><h2>{demo.name}</h2><p>{demo.description}</p><dl class="metrics"><div><dt>Total return</dt><dd>{percent(m.total)}</dd></div><div><dt>Annualized return</dt><dd>{percent(m.annualized)}</dd></div><div><dt>Max drawdown</dt><dd>{percent(m.maxDrawdown)}</dd></div></dl><h2>Net asset value</h2><Chart dates={demo.points.map(p=>p.date)} values={demo.points.map(p=>p.nav)} label="Simulated strategy net asset value chart"/><h2>Drawdown (%)</h2><Chart dates={demo.points.map(p=>p.date)} values={m.drawdowns.map(v=>v*100)} label="Simulated strategy drawdown percentage chart"/><details><summary>Data and methodology</summary><p>Period: {demo.points[0].date} to {demo.points.at(-1)!.date}, with {demo.points.length} observations. These monthly demo observations are not a complete daily series. Maximum drawdown uses the observed points only and may understate drawdowns between observations.</p><p>Total return = ending value / starting value − 1. Annualized return = (ending value / starting value)^(365.25 / elapsed days) − 1. Drawdown = current NAV / running peak NAV − 1; maximum drawdown is the minimum of this series. No additional fees, taxes, or cash flows are modeled. No Sharpe ratio is calculated.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>NAV</th><th>Drawdown</th></tr></thead><tbody>{demo.points.map((p,i)=><tr><td>{p.date}</td><td>{p.nav.toFixed(4)}</td><td>{percent(m.drawdowns[i])}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></details></Layout>